{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program has no `model` block, no parameters, and no sampling statements that score top-level data; `x0` and `tau_x` are context inputs used only for simulation in `generated quantities`.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  vector[2] x0;
  real<lower=0> tau_x;
}

transformed data {
  int<lower=0> M = 2;   // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N = 250; // Number of observations

  vector[2] z0 = [-5, 8]';

  real gamma0 = -7;                          // Intercept
  vector[M] gamma1 = [4, -6]';               // Linear slopes
  matrix[M, M] gamma2 = [ [3, -1], [-1, 1]]; // Quadratic slopes
  real sigma = 0.5;                          // Measurement variability
}

generated quantities {
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix
  array[N] real y;      // Variates

  for (n in 1:N) {
    X[n, 1] = normal_rng(x0[1], tau_x);
    X[n, 2] = normal_rng(x0[2], tau_x);
    y[n] = normal_rng(  gamma0
                      + (X[n] - z0') * gamma1
                      + (X[n] - z0') * gamma2 * (X[n] - z0')'
                      + pow(X[n, 1] / 2.75 - 0, 3) + pow(X[n, 2] / 2.25 - 0, 3), sigma);
  }
}

